SECTION 2 — AI/ML RESTRICTIONS

Notwithstanding Section 1, the Software, in whole or in part, shall not be
provided as input to, or ingested, read, indexed, embedded, or otherwise
processed by, any AI System. In particular, the following are prohibited:

(a) using the Software to train, pre-train, fine-tune, continue training,
    reinforce, or distill a model;

(b) including the Software in any training or evaluation dataset, benchmark,
    embedding, vector database, index, or retrieval/RAG system used by an AI
    System;

(c) processing the Software with an AI System for inference, analysis,
    summarization, translation, transformation, completion, recommendation,
    or generation, including via code-completion systems, AI coding
    assistants, or autonomous/agentic coding systems, whether the Software
    is provided directly, as prompt or context, or via a retrieval,
    indexing, caching, or storage mechanism;

(d) using an AI System to create a derivative work of the Software, to
    extract, reproduce, port, refactor, rewrite, or extend any portion of
    the Software, or to incorporate any output of an AI System that is based
    on, derived from, or contains any portion of the Software into this or
    any other work or project.


SECTION 3 — DEFINITIONS

"AI System" means any software, product, or service that uses machine
learning, neural networks, large language models, or other models trained on
data to generate, complete, transform, analyze, classify, or make
predictions about content, including any tool that incorporates such a
system.

Ordinary deterministic development tools that do not use machine learning on
the Software — including compilers, interpreters, linkers, build systems,
version control systems, package managers, text editors, syntax
highlighting, linters, formatters, and static analysis tools — are not AI
Systems and are not restricted by Section 2.

"Derivative work" has the meaning given by applicable copyright law and, for
the avoidance of doubt, additionally includes any output of an AI System
produced using the Software as input.


